#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147173 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147394 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b754e55b-59fa-50de-b2f9-0444c3177041" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Stand-Alone Exponents"}] :question/id #uuid "6d89587f-dacf-5ce3-95f0-9dd51d307af8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14188" :question/problem "Evaluate $4^2 +(5-3).$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n4^2\\,+\\underbrace{(5-3)}_{\\large\\color{blue} 2}  =4^2\\,+ {\\color{blue} 2}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n\\overbrace{4^2}^{\\large\\color{red} 16}+2 = {\\color{red} 16}+2\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n16+2 = 18\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n4^2 +(5-3)=18.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147174 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0704b3c4-42a9-50f8-a73c-b938a22b3cad" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "b035d6d2-aaca-5ea3-8d34-1748b6acfcd6" :question/math-academy-id "e-14191" :question/problem "Calculate $28\\div(7-5)^2.$" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n28\\div \\underbrace{(7-5)}_{\\large\\color{blue} 2}{}^2   =28\\div {\\color{blue} 2}^2\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we compute the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n28\\div\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{red} 4} =28\\div {\\color{red} 4}\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **D**ivision:\n\n$$\n28\\div 4 =7\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n28\\div(7-5)^2=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147175 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147396 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d7cee42-a91c-5053-8e50-3078d31cc772" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Inside Parentheses"}] :question/id #uuid "ef92369b-53e8-56ec-b1f2-ee36dbf13839" :question/math-academy-id "e-14193" :question/problem "Evaluate $5\\times \\left(3+2^2\\right).$" :question/worked-solution "According to PEMDAS, we should first calculate the expression inside the **P**arentheses: $\\left(3+2^2\\right).$\n\nTo evaluate $\\left(3+2^2\\right),$ we should again apply PEMDAS. We start with the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n3\\,+\\overbrace{2^2}^{\\large\\color{blue} 4} =3+ {\\color{blue} 4}\n$$\n\nThen, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n3 + 4 =  {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\nSo we have:\n\n$$\n5\\times \\underbrace{\\left(3+2^2\\right)}_{\\large\\color{red} 7}  =5\\times {\\color{red} 7}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that we have calculated the expression inside the **P**arentheses, we can finally move on to the **M**ultiplication:\n\n$$\n5 \\times 7 = 35\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n5\\times\\left(3+2^2\\right)=35.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478426 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0704b3c4-42a9-50f8-a73c-b938a22b3cad" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa603b27-1abf-58e7-b261-8c7b04bd66ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa603b27-1abf-58e7-b261-8c7b04bd66ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478233} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc07ed4d-8672-5e65-a823-f8558de87043" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478364}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c874a34-8c6f-5943-b20d-99a608c0c078" :question/math-academy-id "q-212255" :question/problem "$(1+5)^{2}+{4}^{3}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use PEMDAS. We start with the **P**arentheses:\n\n$$\n{{(1+5)}_{⏟}}_{6}{}^{2}+{4}^{3}={6}^{2}+{4}^{3}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we find the **E**xponents:\n\n$$\n\\overset{36}{\\overset{⏞}{{6}^{2}}}+\\overset{64}{\\overset{⏞}{{4}^{3}}}=36+64\n$$\n\nFinally, we perform the **A**ddition:\n\n$$\n36+64=100\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147395 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0704b3c4-42a9-50f8-a73c-b938a22b3cad" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Expressions With Exponents Outside Parentheses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2379eba6-c09a-5710-ac2a-ffe2ab4644c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477805} {:answer/id #uuid "70df72ff-5c30-57ea-9ca8-00b7ce34fefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477972} {:answer/id #uuid "ae997179-a2f5-5d36-9f9a-17371a9572a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478075} {:answer/id #uuid "e0cb04ef-86a7-57ba-a45a-a600e3139dbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478177} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9002ab-01ce-5c78-9a1f-b0a5b8fecf6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae997179-a2f5-5d36-9f9a-17371a9572a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478075} :answer-field/id #uuid "66ad66da-e7ce-51f3-bdaf-5fa63c21001e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478293}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72d8229d-fbfb